WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.282
Local processing can keep images and outputs under direct control,

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:07.209
but deployment still needs a data policy.

00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:10.555
Define storage, retention, access, export, logs, and deletion.

00:00:10.555 --> 00:00:15.992
Avoid sending images to external services unless that flow is approved and transparent.

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:21.428
Review the model and runtime licenses for the intended use, distribution, and modification.

00:00:21.428 --> 00:00:25.610
Track model source, file integrity, version, prompt template, and dependencies.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:29.374
Treat model updates as software changes with regression testing.

00:00:29.374 --> 00:00:33.974
Operational workflows need queues, timeouts, retries, alert routing, and human review.

00:00:33.974 --> 00:00:38.993
A fallback model or simpler pipeline can preserve service when the preferred

00:00:38.993 --> 00:00:41.084
model exceeds memory or fails,

00:00:41.084 --> 00:00:44.011
but the system should label changed capability.

00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:48.193
Cost includes hardware, power, cooling, storage, administration, and reviewer time.

00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:52.793
A larger model may cost more operationally without improving the task.

00:00:52.793 --> 00:00:56.557
Monitor throughput, completion, latency, memory pressure, temperature, queue depth,

00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:57.811
and output quality.

00:00:57.811 --> 00:01:00.321
Do not blindly trust model output.

00:01:00.321 --> 00:01:04.921
Important decisions should link back to visible evidence and accountable review.

00:01:04.921 --> 00:01:09.521
Local vision systems should not be used for covert stalking, harassment,

00:01:09.521 --> 00:01:13.285
inappropriate surveillance, or identifying private individuals without lawful authority.

00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:18.721
Reevaluate over time as cameras, documents, use cases, models, drivers, and runtimes change.

00:01:18.721 --> 00:01:21.649
Keep a known-good configuration and rollback path.

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:23.322
Deployment success means stable,

00:01:23.322 --> 00:01:28.340
privacy-conscious assistance that remains understandable when the model is wrong or unavailable.
